            <div xml:id="d730">

                <pb facs="0834" n="824" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg824"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.0093/9–1648: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-09-16T11:00:00+09:00">September 16,
                            1948—11 a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 16—1:16 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1702. Redeptel 1302, September 13, 3 p. m. Appropriate instructions have been
                    issued to Consulates. Embassy is most appreciative of Department’s explanation
                    of action which was not clear to Embassy and of the reasons, therefore, of which
                    it was not previously aware.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
